<Base title="About Ivan" description="35 years fixing problems solo. Now trying AI tools for solo business owners.">
  <h1>Hi, I’m Ivan.</h1>
  <p class="lead">I spent 35 years fixing problems in people’s homes, working on my own.</p>
  <p>I ran a one-man computer repair business and went to my clients’ homes. I learned two things. Problems come back when people don’t understand why they happened, so I always explained the why, to make sure I wouldn’t be called back for the same mistake. And finding clients is harder than doing the work. I faced that second problem alone for years.</p>
  <h2>Why I try AI tools</h2>
  <p>Today, AI tools can lighten a solo owner’s load: finding clients, saving time, and handing off the jobs you don’t enjoy so you can focus on the work you love. I try each tool myself, on a real project, and I give you my personal opinion on whether it would be good for you and how to make it fit the way you work.</p>
  <h2>What you can expect</h2>
  <p>Honest opinions, including when a tool isn’t good. Clear explanations without jargon. When I really like a tool, I’ll tell you why, with specifics. And a verdict at the end of every review: for you, or not for you, with reasons.</p>
  <h2>Who this is for</h2>
  <p>Business owners working alone, in any trade or profession, who want to spend less time on the tasks around the work and more on the work itself. If you like to understand why something works before you trust it, you’ll feel at home here.</p>
  <p class="note">Some links here are affiliate links. <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Read how I handle them</a>.</p>
</Base>
